## Bugs / behavior

1. `sp play --seed-track` still applies text `--min-score` cutoff to raw cosine scores. `rank_by_similarity` returns cosine blend, not upper-cluster fit. Current CLI cutoff defaults to `0.9`, so this can silently drop seed matches. Use separate seed cutoff or skip text cutoff in seed mode.
2. `sp index` can fail on symlinked audio outside library root: `relative_posix` resolves file symlink then `relative_to(root)` raises. Internal aliases can also collapse to target path. Preserve path relative to root without resolving file.
3. `sp play -o -` prints preview lines, not m3u8, despite help text. Render playlist to stdout.
4. Re-indexing another root into same DB can keep old vectors when relative paths match; reject changed root or force rescan.
5. Indexing overwrites MODEL metadata without validating old model. Check stored model before indexing unless rescan.
6. `audio/windowing.py`: short tracks under window size are rejected despite `MIN_WINDOW_SECONDS`; final partial window dropped; failure text says “too short or silent” although silent tracks are retained.
7. Failed `--rescan` can leave old track row plus failure row; status counts both.

## Minor / cleanup

- `query/search.py`: `starts` / `ends` computed twice; second computation is dead.
- `query/search.py`: mean cosine is recomputed from windows although stored mean vector can provide it.
- `--seed-track` accepts only exact indexed relative path; `sp describe` resolves absolute and cwd-relative paths. Positional query is still required in seed mode and only used for playlist filename.
- `index_cmd.py`: `DecodeError` and generic `Exception` handlers duplicate behavior.
- `index_cmd.py`: per-file `has_track` queries could use one `track_rel_paths()` fetch.
- `--min-score >= 1.0` is not validated.

Historical checks: legacy `vocab_calibration_score` batching/offset bookkeeping, comparison broadcast, and exclusion handling looked correct. Silence-trim boundaries, window offsets, vector normalization, upsert delete/insert order, and `embed_windows` batch slicing also looked correct.
